							4 November, 1988.

Hi,

	This is the readme file for the source code diskette.

	On this diskette, you will find all the C source and include files
necessary to make fishNET go.

	To compile it in MSDOS systems with Microsoft compilers, just
type

			make fishNET

which will use the program maintenance utility to make the code.

	If your system doesn't have an 80(1/2/3)87, you will need to edit
the makefile, called fishNET, and remove the ``-FPi87'' directive. Also,
you will need to replace the ``qcl'' compiler name with ``cl'' if you want
to use the full Microsoft compiler instead of the default QuickC.

	For Unix systems, enter the Makefile as shown in the thesis document
in Appendix A.

	For MSDOS systems with an 80(1/2/3)87, object (*.obj) and executable
(*.exe) files are given. NOTE again that you MUST recompile them without the
``-FPi87'' directive if you don't have a coprocessor.

	Good luck with fishNET.

Scott MacGibbon.

