P.P.S. I have also included 2 extra files on this diskette. One is a program
called ``mtbf'' which will give you the mean time between failure for a system.
See the thesis, chapter 8, and reference [28] for more information.

	The other is a program called ``erate'' which is a very crude program
for calculating the total error as used in the thesis for chapters 7 and 8.
It compares the entered data file with dat\huge.out, or so I think from
memory. Anyway, I just bashed it out in a hurry, and it is ripe for
enhancement (especially with regard to the file used for comparison). 
Note that its calculation of total error is twice that calculated
in chapter 2, because I didn't worry about multiply it by 1/2 for comparison
purposes in the experimental chapters. Also, you will need to link to some
of the object modules of fishNET for the file parsing routines. The modules
that you will have to link to have are the same ones whose ``.h'' files are
included at the start of the file. Don't worry about the link errors, as those
routines aren't called by ``erate''.

	Once again, they are compiled for 80(1/2/3)87 systems.

